      "fair4ml:intendedUse": "The model is intended for a reproducible course experiment that demonstrates how road collision severity can be predicted from STATS19 tabular data and documented with FAIR metadata. It may support retrospective analysis and educational comparison of open-science machine-learning workflows.",
      "fair4ml:modelRisksBiasLimitations": "The model should not be used for live emergency dispatch, clinical triage, policing, insurance decisions, or individual-level risk decisions. Fatal collisions are rare in the training and test data, and the resulting performance for the Fatal class is weak despite class balancing. The model uses historical 2023 Great Britain STATS19 records and may not generalise to other years, countries, reporting practices, or operational settings.",
      "fair4ml:ethicalSocial": "Predictions concern road casualties and should be interpreted cautiously. The model can reproduce historical reporting biases and class imbalance in STATS19. Any operational use would require additional validation, governance, monitoring, and human oversight.",
